   "reading": "THE FOUR FRAMEWORKS ON CHATGPT, SIGNED OUT: the common problem, 'how an originating act becomes transmissible across time when its original author, source, or historical position is absent, obscured, or structurally unavailable'; the synthesis, 'An intellectual origin can survive its originating agent, distribute itself across multiple authors or texts, and become operative in future readers, while the very process that preserves its content can simultaneously erase its provenance.'; and the evidentiary table's 'most vulnerable' transitions, among them 'From a possible future-reader position t",
